5,0 $ Pileus white, pale pink. Stipe white, yellow-white below: $ M. albido-rosea
5,6 $ Pileus with darker colours
6,0 $ Clamp connections absent. Growing on fallen Picea cones in the spring: $ M. strobilicola
6,7 $ Clamp connections present
7,0 $ Pileus grey-brown to cream brown. Odour strongly of chloride. Cheilocystidia 27-40 µm long, subcylindrical, utriform or clavate. Spores 7.3-9.0 x 4.6-5.4 µm: $ M. caliginosa
7,8 $ Pileus dark brown to blackish
8,0 $ Cheilocystidia 20-60 µm long, clavate to fusiform. Terrestrial: $ M. ustalis (4-spored)
8,0 $ Cheilocystidia 57-103 µm long, strongly protruding, fusiform or sublageniform. Growing on decaying wood of deciduous trees: $ M. algeriensis
9,10 $ Pileus dark brown to blackish
9,11 $ Pileus paler grey-brown
10,0 $ Cheilocystidia 20-60 µm long, clavate to fusiform. Terrestrial: $ M. ustalis (2-spored)
10,0 $ Cheilocystidia 57-103 µm long, strongly protruding, fusiform or sublageniform. Growing on decaying wood of deciduous trees: $ M. algeriensis
11,0 $ Cheilocystidia 25-45 x 4-6 µm, sinuous, flexuous, smooth to coarsely furcate. Terrestrial: $ M. maurella
11,0 $ Cheilocystidia 40-110 x 9-22 µm, fusiform, lageniform, subcylindrical or clavate, smooth. On decaying wood of deciduous trees.: $ M. niveipes
12,0 $ Pileus white, growing cespitose on decaying wood of conifers: $ M. laevigata
12,13 $ Pileus differently coloured.
13,0 $ Hyphae of the pileipellis and the cortical layer of the stipe embedded in gelatinous matter. Pileus dark sepia brown. Cespitose on coniferous wood: $ M. stipata
13,14 $ Hyphae og the pileipellis and the cortical layer of the stipe not gelatinized. Occuring in the spring.
14,0 $ Pileus at first blackish brown, then sepia brown, reddish brown to grey brown, lamellae grey, stipe slightly paler than the pileus. On decaying stµmp of Pinus: $ M. tephrophylla
14,0 $ Pileus pale dingy pinkish brown, lamellae pink, stipe pale brownish white with a slight yellowish tint. On decayed wood of Fagus: $ M. lignivora
14,0 $ Pileus vinous purplish brown, lamellae whitish, stipe ochraceous yellow. On decayed wood of deciduous tree. : $ M. aculeata

KEY 2.Hyphae of the pileipellis smooth. Hyphae of the cortical layer of the stipe with excrescences.

